To solve the problem, we start by expressing the polynomial \( P \) as \( P(x) = x \cdot Q(x) \), where \( Q \) is another polynomial with integer coefficients. Given that \( \gcd(P(0), P(1), P(2), \ldots) = 1 \), it follows that \( \gcd(Q(0), Q(1), Q(2), \ldots) = 1 \).

