To find a real number \( t \) such that for any set of 120 points \( P_1, \ldots, P_{120} \) on the boundary of a unit square, there exists a point \( Q \) on this boundary with \( |P_1Q| + |P_2Q| + \cdots + |P_{120}Q| = t \).

