The complete solution is all positive integers \(a, n \ge 1\) such that either \(a = 1\), \(a = 2\), \(a = 2^k - 1\), or \(a = 2\) with \(n = 6\). Thus, the solution set is:

$$
(a, n) = (1, n) \text{ for any } n \ge 1, \quad (2, 6), \quad \text{and} \quad (2^k - 1, 2) \text{ for } k \ge 2.
$$

The final answer is:

\boxed{(2, 6), (2^k - 1, 2), (1, n) \text{ for any } n \ge 1}
